-- title:
--   Natural filtration of a real process and submartingales with respect to a family of $\sigma$-algebras
-- statement:
--   For a real process $X=(X_t)_{t\ge0}$ on $(\Omega,\mathcal F,P)$, its natural filtration is $\mathcal F^X_s=\sigma(X_u:u\le s)$. A process $X$ is a **submartingale** with respect to a nondecreasing family $(\mathcal G_t)$ of sub-σ-algebras of $\mathcal F$ if each $X_t$ is $\mathcal G_t$-measurable and integrable and
--
--   $$
--   X_s\le E[X_t\mid\mathcal G_s]\quad\text{a.s., }s\le t .
--   $$
--
--   Used in Lemma 6.3.
--
--   **Formalization Note** The paper's augmented natural filtration also contains the $P$-null sets; augmentation changes no conditional expectation up to a.e. equality, so (sub)martingale properties are the same. The shape matches `MartingaleHT.InfiniteServer.IsMartingaleWrt`.
-- source:
--   Yu and Perry, Many-Server Heavy-Traffic Limits for Queueing Systems with Perfectly Correlated Service and Patience Times, arXiv:2008.12890v1, §6.1, p.24 (Lemma 6.3)

import Mathlib

open MeasureTheory
open scoped NNReal

namespace PerfCorrMSQ

/-!
The natural filtration of a real process indexed by `ℝ≥0`, and submartingales with respect to
a family of σ-algebras (used in Lemma 6.3 of Yu–Perry, arXiv:2008.12890v1, p.24).
-/

/-- The **natural filtration** of `X`: at time `s`, the σ-algebra generated by `X(u)`, `u ≤ s`.

**Formalization Note.** The paper's "augmented natural filtration" also contains the `P`-null
sets; augmenting by null sets does not change conditional expectations up to a.e. equality, so
(sub)martingale properties are the same for both. -/
def natFiltr {Ω : Type*} (X : ℝ≥0 → Ω → ℝ) (s : ℝ≥0) : MeasurableSpace Ω :=
  ⨆ (u : ℝ≥0) (_ : u ≤ s), MeasurableSpace.comap (X u) inferInstance

/-- `X` is a **submartingale with respect to `𝓖`** on `(Ω, P)`: `𝓖` is a nondecreasing family of
sub-σ-algebras of the ambient σ-algebra, each `X(t)` is `𝓖(t)`-measurable and integrable, and
`X(s) ≤ E[X(t) | 𝓖(s)]` almost surely for `s ≤ t`. (Same shape as
`MartingaleHT.InfiniteServer.IsMartingaleWrt`.) -/
def IsSubmartingaleWrt {Ω : Type*} [mΩ : MeasurableSpace Ω] (𝓖 : ℝ≥0 → MeasurableSpace Ω)
    (P : Measure Ω) (X : ℝ≥0 → Ω → ℝ) : Prop :=
  Monotone 𝓖 ∧ (∀ t, 𝓖 t ≤ mΩ) ∧ (∀ t, StronglyMeasurable[𝓖 t] (X t)) ∧
  (∀ t, Integrable (X t) P) ∧ ∀ s t : ℝ≥0, s ≤ t → X s ≤ᵐ[P] P[X t | 𝓖 s]

end PerfCorrMSQ


